        <mxCell id="FuzdddfIqP1HJb-b7X9h-1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;spacing=6;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;" value="&lt;b&gt;Design notes (consistent with the Class Diagram)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. &lt;b&gt;Original vs processed:&lt;/b&gt; ENTRY.original_content (= Entry.journal) is WRITE-ONCE and never updated. Every processed or edited text is a new append-only ENTRY_VERSION row (original_text snapshot + final_text).&lt;br&gt;2. &lt;b&gt;Hash chain:&lt;/b&gt; ENTRY_VERSION.previous_hash → current_hash, linked per owner in chain_seq order (HashChainService.verifyOwnerChain). The first link uses GENESIS_HASH as previous_hash.&lt;br&gt;3. &lt;b&gt;Death trigger:&lt;/b&gt; DEATH_TRIGGER.state is the single source of truth. Owner.isDeceased maps to OWNER.is_deceased, a derived value (state = CONFIRMED), not stored separately.&lt;br&gt;4. &lt;b&gt;Access rules:&lt;/b&gt; PROTOCOL.source_text (sourceText) is compiled into POLICY_FACT rows (compiledFacts); GRANT holds action / effect / topic per beneficiary.&lt;br&gt;5. &lt;b&gt;BENEFICIARY (TrustedPerson):&lt;/b&gt; surrogate PK beneficiary_id with UNIQUE (owner_id, trusted_person_id), so one user can be trusted by several owners. Every FK to BENEFICIARY targets BENEFICIARY.beneficiary_id (GRANT.beneficiary_id, INVITATION.beneficiary_id, LEGACY_ACCESS_REQUEST.beneficiary_id; recipient_id = Class Diagram recipientId). Same-owner scope: a row referencing BENEFICIARY must carry the same owner_id as that beneficiary (enforced by composite FK (owner_id, beneficiary_id) or constraint).&lt;br&gt;6. &lt;b&gt;Class → table:&lt;/b&gt; TrustedPerson → BENEFICIARY, RecipientAccess → INVITATION, LetterEntry → LETTER_ENTRY (subtype of ENTRY), LetterOfWishes → LETTER_OF_WISHES (subtype of LEGACY_ITEM), LegacyItem.recipientId → LEGACY_ITEM_RECIPIENT, Entry.tags → ENTRY_TAG, Entry.people → PERSON via STAR_ENTRY." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="190" width="2910" x="190" y="210" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="k3p6Ns2om5Yv_2ucB69N-1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;fontSize=12;align=left;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="Colors: blue = identity &amp;amp; account, green = diary &amp;amp; hash chain, yellow = people &amp;amp; memory, orange = privacy protocols &amp;amp; access, purple = legacy &amp;amp; death trigger. PK = primary key, FK = foreign key (→ referenced table), UK = unique. Each line starts at the parent&#39;s primary key (one side) and ends at the child&#39;s FK row (crow&#39;s foot = many, circle = optional). owner_id on ENTRY, GRANT and CONSTELLATION_STAR also points to OWNER (scope FK, line not drawn to keep the diagram readable)." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="50" width="2910" x="230" y="170" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
